Anthropic's CCAR-F (Claude Certified Architect – Foundations) and CCAR-P (Claude Certified Architect – Professional) certifications are valuable learning milestones for professionals interested in Claude AI, AI architecture, and agentic AI development.

This repository is intended to help candidates explore certification topics, organize their preparation, and discover useful learning resources.

CCAR-F Certification Preparation

The CCAR-F preparation journey should begin with a strong understanding of Claude and its ecosystem.

Important topics to study include:

Claude models and capabilities

Claude API fundamentals

Prompt engineering and context management

Tool use and function calling

Model Context Protocol (MCP)

AI safety and responsible AI

Claude application architecture

CCAR-P Certification Preparation

CCAR-P preparation requires deeper technical understanding and practical experience.

Recommended study areas:

Advanced Claude API integration

Multi-agent architecture

Agentic workflows

MCP integrations

Multi-tool orchestration

AI application evaluation

Reliability and security

Production-ready AI solutions

Recommended Study Resources

Candidates should prioritize official Anthropic documentation, learning courses, and practical development exercises.

Additional practice resources can also help candidates evaluate their knowledge. During my preparation, I explored Pass4Surexams for supplementary CCAR-F and CCAR-P PDF study materials and test engine practice.

Combining documentation, hands-on projects, and practice questions can make preparation more structured.

Practical Projects to Build

Here are some useful project ideas for candidates:

Build a Claude-powered research assistant.

Create an MCP-connected application.

Develop a multi-tool AI agent.

Build a structured data extraction workflow.

Implement an AI evaluation pipeline.

